          "timestamp": "2026-11-18T10:21:32-07:00",
          "message": "fix(git): a failed ask is a read that never started; the ask runs in the read's directory; forge reads unset GH_REPO (a623)\n"
        },
        {
          "sha": "5948360b1a83bbca3d9997dab3cba7b32c3af819",
          "author_name": "Brandon Fryslie",
          "author_email": "530235+brandon-fryslie@users.noreply.github.com",
          "timestamp": "2026-11-18T10:07:44-07:00",
          "message": "fix(git): a git or forge read unsets the repository variables of the shell that spawned the daemon (a623)\n\nEvery git read, forge CLI launch and the doctor's forge probe now launch\nthrough one asker that unsets the variables `git rev-parse\n--local-env-vars` names, asked of git once. The daemon's environment is\nthe spawning shell's, so a hook's or vcsh's GIT_DIR pointed every\nsession's read at that shell's repository. An ask that fails is the\nread's own failed launch, never a read with the variables.\n"
        }
      ]
